    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Excellent! The fix is confirmed to be working. The `--ci` flag is now properly passed through to the `frai-gate` command, creating both the `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` files.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was caused by two issues:\n\n1. **Global option consumption**: The main `frai` program defined a `--ci` option globally, which Commander was consuming before passing arguments to the `gate` subcommand. This meant the `--ci` flag never reached the gate subcommand handler.\n\n2. **Incomplete argument reconstruction**: Even after the first fix, the gate command handler wasn't capturing the `options` parameter from Commander, so it couldn't include unknown options in the spawned `frai-gate` command.\n\n**The fix involved two changes to `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:**\n\n1. Added `.passThroughOptions()` to the main program to tell Commander to pass through all options to subcommands without consuming them at the global level (line 614).\n\n2. Updated the gate command's action handler to:\n   - Accept the `options` parameter in addition to `args`\n   - Iterate through the options and reconstruct command-line flags\n   - Pass the complete argument list to the spawned `frai-gate` process\n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and the fix has been verified to work correctly.",
